.\" jailops-priv.8, installed as /usr/local/share/man/man8/jailops-priv.8
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt JAILOPS-PRIV 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailops-priv
.Nd the privileged helper of JailOps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Cm check-config
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Cm hook Ar phase jail
.Nm
.Cm init Fl pool Ar pool
.Op Fl dry-run
.Op Ar flags
.Nm
.Op Ar flags
.Cm revert-pending
.Nm
.Cm appliance-init
.Op Fl pool Ar pool
.Op Fl config Ar file
.Op Fl dry-run
.Nm
.Cm setup-token
.Op Fl socket Ar path
.Op Fl wait Ar duration
.Op Fl syslog
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs as root and performs, for
.Xr jailopsd 8 ,
a fixed list of typed operations: ZFS datasets and snapshots below the storage
roots and the keys of encrypted jail volumes (the passphrase on standard input),
jails, interfaces and bridges, pf anchors, a few sysctls, downloads of
images and the files the daemon may read.
Everything else is refused, and every request is written to the audit log.
The daemon connects over a unix socket owned by root and the group
.Sy jailops ,
mode 0660; only the configured users and groups may connect.
.Pp
Flags are written with one dash, as in
.Fl pool ;
two dashes
.Pq Fl -pool
are read the same.
This differs from
.Xr jailops 1 ,
whose long flags take two dashes.
.Pp
Without a command the helper serves on its socket.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm check-config
Validate the configuration and the storage file, print the effective storage
roots (with the reason a root is inactive), the directories, the interface
prefixes, the admin policy, the fixed binaries and every allow-list.
Inactive roots are warnings: a pool may not be imported yet.
.It Cm hook Ar phase jail
Run one jail hook and exit.
The rendered jail.conf files call this from their exec.* lines;
.Ar phase
is
.Cm prestart , poststart , prestop
or
.Cm poststop .
.It Cm init Fl pool Ar pool
The one-time setup of a host: the user and group, the storage root dataset
.Pa pool/jailops
mounted at
.Pa /usr/local/jailops ,
the state dataset mounted at
.Pa /var/db/jailops/state
and owned by the daemon's user, the directories, and the two configuration
files.
Everything is idempotent; what exists is left as it is and said so.
Flags:
.Fl dataset ,
.Fl mount ,
.Fl user ,
.Fl group ,
.Fl etc ,
.Fl data-dir ,
.Fl web
(turn the web console on in the daemon's configuration),
.Fl web-address
(its TLS listener, default :39110) and
.Fl dry-run
(say what would be done and do nothing; needs no root).
.It Cm revert-pending
Put back the snapshot of a host change that waits for its confirmation
(commit confirmed of host management, docs/appliance.md), files only, and end
its record; do nothing when no change waits.
The rc.d script
.Pa jailops_revert
runs it at boot, before
.Sy netif
and
.Sy pf ,
so an unconfirmed change never survives a reboot.
When the helper serves, it does the same on its own: it re-arms the timer of a
pending change at start, or reverts at once when the deadline passed while it
was not running.
.It Cm appliance-init
The first start of an appliance (docs/appliance.md): run by the rc.d script
when
.Va jailops_appliance
is set and the configuration file does not exist.
It does what
.Cm init
does, on
.Fl pool
(from
.Va jailops_pool )
or, without it, on the pool of the root file system
.Pq Ql zfs list -H -o name / .
It refuses a pool that already holds a dataset with
.Sy jailops:managed=on
other than
.Pa pool/jailops ,
and does nothing when the configuration file exists.
Every command it runs and every file it writes is logged to syslog.
.It Cm setup-token
Ask the daemon, over its unix socket and as root, for a new one-time setup
token of the first administrator, and print it with the addresses of the web
console.
The token replaces the one before, is valid for 24 hours and is used up by
the first administrator it creates.
.Fl wait
waits for the socket of a daemon that is starting;
.Fl syslog
also logs the token and the addresses with the facility
.Sy authpriv
(on
.Fx
.Pa /var/log/auth.log ,
readable by root only).
The rc.d script of
.Xr jailopsd 8
runs it after every start in appliance mode and writes its output to
.Pa /dev/console .
.It Cm version
Print the version and the protocol version.
.Fl -version
does the same.
.El
.Pp
The flags, which are also the keys of the configuration file
.Po except
.Fl appliance-modules ,
which only the rc.d script passes
.Pc :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl appliance-modules Ar list
The host management modules
.Va jailops_appliance
of
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
turns on, comma separated, or
.Sy all .
They are added to
.Sy host-manage ;
.Cm check-config
prints both lists.
.It Fl config Ar file
The configuration file: lines of
.Ar key No = Ar value
named like the flags.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf ;
a missing default file is not an error.
The file must be owned by root and not writable by group or others.
.It Fl socket Ar path
The unix socket, default
.Pa /var/run/jailops-priv/priv.sock .
Its directory belongs to root, mode 0710 with the group of the socket,
so the daemon can reach the socket but put nothing in its place.
The former default
.Pa /var/run/jailops/priv.sock
is read as this path.
.It Fl group Ar name , Fl mode Ar octal
The group that owns the socket (default
.Sy jailops )
and its mode (default 0660; others may have no access).
.It Fl allow-user Ar name , Fl allow-group Ar name
A user (the daemon's) or a group allowed to connect.
Repeatable, comma separated.
At least one is required to serve.
.It Fl storage-root Ar dataset
A storage root dataset fixed in the file, for example
.Pa tank/jailops
(repeatable); more are registered at run time and kept in the storage file.
A pool's top dataset is refused unless
.Fl allow-pool-root
is set.
.It Fl storage-file Ar path
The file that persists the storage roots registered at run time, default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.d/storage.conf
(root-owned, mode 0600).
.It Xo
.Fl mount-base Ar dir , Fl state-dir Ar dir ,
.Fl conf-dir Ar dir , Fl work-dir Ar dir
.Xc
The mount point the storage roots are checked against, the state directory
(required; by default
.Pa mount-base/state ) ,
the directory of the rendered jail.conf files (default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jails )
and the daemon's scratch directory for image builds.
.It Fl helper-path Ar path
The path the jail.conf hooks call, default
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/jailops-priv .
.It Fl if-prefix Ar prefix
An interface name prefix owned by JailOps (default
.Sy jo ) .
.It Fl ndp-proxy Ar uplink=prefix,...
An uplink the IPv6 proxy may use and the prefixes it may answer for
(repeatable).
.It Fl sysctl Ar name , Fl fetch-host Ar host , Fl image-mirror Ar dir
An extra sysctl readable through the helper, a host images may be fetched
from over https, a local directory of image archives.
.It Xo
.Fl admin-raw-param , Fl admin-allow-flag , Fl admin-devfs-ruleset ,
.Fl admin-host-mount , Fl admin-zfs-prop , Fl admin-routes ,
.Fl admin-raw-pf , Fl admin-resume-send
.Xc
The admin policy: what an administrator of the daemon may set beyond the
built-in rules.
.It Fl wireguard-routes Ar cidr
A network a WireGuard tunnel may route into itself although the route is
wider than a /8 (/16 for IPv6) or covers an address of the host, its default
gateway, a resolver, loopback, link-local or multicast (repeatable).
Without it, or
.Fl admin-routes ,
such routes are refused.
.It Fl log Ar stderr | syslog
The audit log destination.
Default stderr, or syslog with
.Fl daemon .
.It Fl pidfile Ar path
Write the process id here.
.It Fl daemon
Detach from the terminal.
The rc.d script uses
.Xr daemon 8
instead.
.It Fl dev
Development: do not require root, allow the invoking user.
.El
.Sh RC.CONF
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailops_priv
runs the helper under
.Xr daemon 8
with
.Fl log Ar syslog ;
it requires
.Sy zfs ,
.Sy jailops_revert
and
.Sy syslogd
(the audit lines go to syslog) and runs before
.Sy jailopsd ,
which stops before it at shutdown.
.Xr daemon 8
supervises the helper: when it exits without being stopped, a crash or
.Dv SIGKILL ,
it is started again after five seconds, and that start re-arms a pending host
change as any start does.
.Cm stop
ends the supervisor, which stops the helper;
.Cm status
prints the pid of the helper, or that the supervisor is about to start it
again.
Stopping the helper does not stop
.Xr jailopsd 8 :
the daemon answers
.Pa /readyz
with
.Dq not ready: helper ,
its requests to the helper fail meanwhile, and it reconnects once the helper
is back.
Jails keep running while the helper restarts.
.Pp
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailops_revert
runs
.Cm revert-pending
once at boot, after
.Sy FILESYSTEMS
and before
.Sy netif ,
.Sy pf
and
.Sy jailops_priv ,
whenever
.Va jailops_priv_enable
is set.
.Bl -tag -width jailops_priv_config
.It Va jailops_priv_enable
Set to
.Dq YES
to start the helper at boot.
.It Va jailops_priv_config
The configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf .
.It Va jailops_appliance
.Dq YES
turns appliance mode on: the script passes
.Fl appliance-modules
with the modules of
.Va jailops_appliance_modules ,
which the helper changes besides those
.Sy host-manage
of the configuration file lists, and at the first start, without the
configuration file, it runs
.Cm appliance-init .
.Xr jailopsd 8
reads the same variables.
.It Va jailops_appliance_modules
The host management modules of appliance mode, separated by spaces.
Default: all modules of this version
.Pq Sy identity firewall .
.It Va jailops_pool
The pool
.Cm appliance-init
sets up.
Default: the pool of the root file system.
.El
.Pp
.Va jailops_appliance
is no weaker than
.Sy host-manage
in
.Pa priv.conf :
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
belongs to root like
.Pa priv.conf ,
it is read when the helper starts and never by the daemon, and whoever can
write it is root already.
The daemon cannot switch appliance mode on.
.Pp
The configuration is validated, and the effective roots printed, with
.Dl service jailops_priv checkconfig
and a start refuses a configuration that does not validate.
The storage file is reread with
.Dl service jailops_priv reload
which sends
.Dv SIGHUP
to the helper.
After an upgrade of the package, restart the pair, which stops
.Xr jailopsd 8
first and starts the helper before it:
.Dl service jailopsd restart
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reread the storage file and verify every storage root again.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Stop: the server shuts down and the socket and pidfile are removed.
.It Dv SIGPIPE
Ignored.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.conf
The configuration; the installed sample is
.Pa priv.conf.sample .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/priv.d/storage.conf
The storage roots registered at run time.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-priv/priv.sock
The socket.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-priv.pid
The pid of the helper under rc.d.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-priv-daemon.pid
The pid of its
.Xr daemon 8
supervisor, which the rc.d script starts and stops.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jails
The rendered jail.conf files.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/jailops-priv
The binary, called by the jail.conf hooks.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.Cm check-config
exits 0 with a valid configuration even when a storage root is inactive.
.It 1
Not root (without
.Fl dev ) ,
the socket or pidfile could not be made, another helper is listening, or a
hook failed.
.It 2
Usage, an invalid configuration file or storage file, no allowed peer, a
socket mode others may use, an unknown module in
.Fl appliance-modules ,
or
.Cm init
with bad arguments.
.It 3
.Cm setup-token :
an administrator exists, there is nothing to set up.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jailops 1 ,
.Xr jail.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr jailopsd 8
